::ALG2_U05_L02_GP_Q01::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U05_L02_GP_Q01<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.SYS.3<br><br>Question:<br>What boundary style is used for y &lt; 2x + 1? {
= Dashed#Correct. Strict inequalities use dashed boundaries because equality is not included.
~ Solid#Solid boundaries include equality.
~ No boundary#A graph needs the related boundary line.
~ Only a point#An inequality has a region, not one point.
}

::ALG2_U05_L02_GP_Q02::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U05_L02_GP_Q02<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.SYS.3<br><br>Question:<br>What boundary style is used for y &ge; -x + 3? {
~ Dashed#Dashed means equality is not included.
= Solid#Correct. The symbol &ge; includes equality, so the boundary is included.
~ No boundary#The related equation is still graphed.
~ Only the y-intercept#The full boundary line is needed.
}

::ALG2_U05_L02_GP_Q03::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U05_L02_GP_Q03<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.SYS.3<br><br>Question:<br>Which point satisfies y &le; x + 2? {
~ (1,5)#5 &le; 3 is false.
~ (0,4)#4 &le; 2 is false.
= (1,3)#Correct. Substitute to get 3 &le; 3, which is true.
~ (-1,4)#4 &le; 1 is false.
}

::ALG2_U05_L02_GP_Q04::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U05_L02_GP_Q04<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.SYS.3<br><br>Question:<br>For y &gt; x - 1, which side is shaded? {
~ Below the line#Below would match less than.
~ Only on the line#Strict inequality excludes the boundary line.
~ Neither side#Every inequality shades a half-plane.
= Above the line#Correct. Greater than means y-values above the boundary.
}

::ALG2_U05_L02_GP_Q05::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U05_L02_GP_Q05<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.SYS.3<br><br>Question:<br>What is a feasible region? {
= The overlap of all solution regions#Correct. A system solution must satisfy every inequality.
~ Only the first shaded region#All constraints must be used.
~ Only the boundary line#The feasible region is usually an area.
~ Any point on the coordinate plane#Not every point satisfies the constraints.
}

